  "id": "COMPOUND:16957 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Cinnzeylanin is implicated in the inhibition of DNA polymerase iota through a multi-step mechanism involving its interaction with target entities. The evidence suggests that Cinnzeylanin acts as a target of multiple compounds, including [(1S,2S,4S,7R,8R,9S,10S,12S,13S,16R)-8-acetyloxy-4,7,12,13-tetrahydroxy-2-(2-hydroxypropan-2-yl)-5,9-dimethyl-15-oxatetracyclo[7.6.1.02,6.013,16]hexadec-5-en-10-yl] acetate and 6-Octen-1-ol, 3,7-dimethyl-, 1-acetate, (3R)-, both of which are known to target DNA polymerase iota. This indicates that Cinnzeylanin may interact with DNA polymerase iota through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating its enzymatic activity or by inducing structural changes that disrupt DNA synthesis. The presence of multiple pathways linking Cinnzeylanin to DNA polymerase iota suggests a robust, biologically plausible relationship, supported by the shared target of several compounds. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving the inhibition of DNA polymerase iota, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
